# Geo IP allowlist filter for the Scalingo nginx buildpack.
#
# Loaded from servers.conf.erb ONLY when the Scalingo env var
# ENABLE_GEO_FILTER is set (see the guard there). It is gated behind its own
# env var — separate from ENABLE_MODSECURITY — so the app never boots this rule
# until the GeoIP database below is actually present in the slug; otherwise
# `SecGeoLookupDB` fails to open the file at config-parse time and nginx refuses
# to start, taking the whole app down.
#
# ── PREREQUISITES (must both hold before you set ENABLE_GEO_FILTER) ────────────
#   1. A MaxMind GeoIP2/GeoLite2 *Country* database must exist at the path in
#      SecGeoLookupDB below..
#   2. The buildpack's libmodsecurity must have been built with MaxMindDB
#      support (`--with-maxmind`).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Behaviour: fail-OPEN on indeterminate. If the lookup fails (private/unknown
# IP, DB miss) the `@geoLookup` operator returns false, the chain short-circuits
# and the request is allowed — locking out a legitimate agent is worse than the
# residual risk for a CRM.
SecGeoLookupDB /app/scripts/nginx-geoip-filtering/GeoLite2-Country.mmdb

# One chained rule:
#   - `@geoLookup` on the client IP populates the GEO collection and matches
#     only when the lookup succeeds.
#   - the chained condition denies (403) when the resolved country code is NOT
#     in allowed-countries.txt. `@pmFromFile` matches a pattern that is a
#     substring of the target; since COUNTRY_CODE is exactly 2 chars and every
#     pattern is a 2-char code, the match is effectively exact.
# The client IP is the real client address: servers.conf.erb already sets
# `real_ip_header X-Forwarded-For`, so REMOTE_ADDR is the end user, not the
# Scalingo load balancer.
SecRule REMOTE_ADDR "@geoLookup" \
    "id:1000,\
    phase:1,\
    deny,\
    status:403,\
    t:none,\
    msg:'Geo IP filter: country not in allowlist',\
    logdata:'country=%{geo.country_code} ip=%{remote_addr}',\
    tag:'geo-filter',\
    chain"
    SecRule GEO:COUNTRY_CODE "!@pmFromFile /app/scripts/nginx-geoip-filtering/allowed-countries.txt" "t:none"
